(b) the anti-self-duality argument: what it covers
     4D lift of Drach's first system (CG eq 16 in eq 1): det g = 1, non-flat True, Ricci-flat True, eq(6) upper(SD) False, lower(ASD) True, Kretschmann 0
  ok    B1 4D first-system metric: non-flat, Ricci-flat, ASD (eq 6 lower sign) and not SD
  ok    B2 (computed part) ** = +1 on 2-forms in (2,2), ** = -1 in (1,3)   [{1} {-1}]
     B2 (ARGUED, textbook): in (1,3) * has eigenvalues +-i on real 2-forms, so the SD and ASD halves of a
        real Weyl tensor are complex conjugates. W^- = 0 is a holomorphic condition on the complexified
        metric, so it holds on every real slice; there it forces W = 0, and Ricci-flat + W = 0 is flat,
        contradicting B1. So the 4D first-system metric has NO Lorentzian real form. It carries rank 3, not 4.

     5D rank-4 metric, CG eq 26, order (t, s, x, y, w)
  ok    B3 eq 26 = h + (dw + alpha x dt)^2 with h = CG eq 1, U_base = alpha y + gamma/sqrt(x), no w-leg
     KK base of eq 26: det g = 1, non-flat True, Ricci-flat True, eq(6) upper(SD) False, lower(ASD) True, Kretschmann 0
  ok    B3 the KK base is non-flat, Ricci-flat, ASD, Kretschmann 0
     B3 (ARGUED): g(d_w, d_w) = 1 identically. On any real Lorentzian slice where d_w is real, either d_w is
        spacelike and the base is a Lorentzian real form of h (excluded by B2), or d_w is timelike and
        the base is definite. A definite metric with Kretschmann 0 is flat, but h is not (excluded).
        Slices on which d_w is NOT real are not covered.

     6D rank-4 metric, CG eq 30, order (t, s, x, y, w, u)
  ok    B4 eq 30 = base + (dw + alpha x dt)^2 + (du - dt/sqrt(x))^2 with a CG-eq-1 base   [U_base = alpha*y]
     KK base of eq 30: det g = 1, non-flat False, Ricci-flat True, eq(6) upper(SD) True, lower(ASD) True, Kretschmann 0
  ok    B4 the 6D KK base is FLAT, so the ASD argument does not transfer to eq 30

LABELS
  (a) CONFIRMED
  (b) CORRECTED: no rank-4 (2,2) metric exists in CG (rank 4 lives in 5D (2,3) eq 26 and 6D (2,4) eq 30).
      The ASD argument is sound for the 4D first-system metric (rank 3). It extends to eq 26 only on real
      slices where d_w is real, and not at all to eq 30, whose KK base is flat.

